<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anarawd ap Rhodri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 916</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anarawd ap Rhodri was king of Gwynedd from 878 until his death in 916, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodri-the-great">Rhodri the Great</a>. In 881 he defeated the Mercians at the mouth of the Conwy, a battle the Welsh annals called vengeance for Rhodri. He later allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> and then submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a>, who received him with honour at his court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anarawd-ap-rhodri.jpg" alt="Anarawd ap Rhodri" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Powell · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anarawd_ap_Rhodri.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
